// Plan §42 D5 (owner 2026-10-12, the live-reparse prerequisite): a function
// the session already linked can be defined again, and every call reaches the
// newest body: a later call, a caller compiled earlier, a pointer taken
// earlier (Julia; cling keeps the old body in old callers). A function this
// file defines is redefined the same way.
int twice(int n) { return 2 * n; }
